          %h2#Definitions Definitions
          %p Here are a few concrete realizations of free coproduct completions.
          %h3#ViaIndexedSetsOfObjects Via indexed sets of objects
          %p
            An early reference for the following explicit description is
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Bénabou1985"} Bénabou (1985), §3
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#HuTholen95"} Hu &amp; Tholen (1995), p. 281, 286
          %p
            An explicit description of the free coproduct completion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo ⊔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh_{\sqcup}(\mathcal{C})
            of a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            is:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+pair"} dependent
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pairs"} pairs
                consisting of
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    an index
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi I
                          %mo ∈
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \in
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                %li
                  %p
                    an
                    = succeed "-" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi I
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+set"} indexed set
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %msub
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
