            However, this requires treating
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            as a 2-category, and allowing the 2-cell to be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+natural+transformation"} lax natural transformation
          %h3#AsAGrothendieckConstruction As a Grothendieck construction
          %p
            The following is also pretty immediate and essentially discussed in
            %a{:href => "#Bénabou1985"} Bénabou (1985), §3
            (though without mentioning of the term “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"}> Grothendieck construction
            ”).
          %p
            The free coproduct completion of a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            is equivalently the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
