            %p
          %p
          #FreeDistributiveCategoryMonad.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              It seems plausible, that, more abstractly, Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CoproductCompletionOfCategoryWithProducts"}
              follows because the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-monad"} 2-monad
              for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+product+completion"} free product completion
              would
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributive+law"} distribute
              over the 2-monad for free coproduct cocompletion; the composite 2-monad would exhibit the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+construction"} free
              = succeed "-construction." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributive+category"} distributive category
          %h2#Examples Examples
          %h3#coproduct_completion_of_connected_objects Coproduct completion of connected objects
          %p
            The following examples follow as special cases of Prop.
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoriesOfCoproductsOfConnectedObjects"}
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              The category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+coproduct+completion"} free coproduct completion
              of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+category"} terminal category
          %p
          #SkeletalGroupoids.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skeletal+groupoids"} skeletal groupoids
                form the free coproduct completion of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groups"} groups
              %br/
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-category"} 1-category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skeletal+groupoids"} skeletal groupoids
              among that of all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+groupoids"} strict groupoids
              is the free coproduct completion of the category of 1-object
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping+groupoids"} delooping groupoids
              which (
              %em>
                as
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-categories"} 1-categories
              ) is equivalently the category of
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groups"} groups
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo ⊔
