            %p
              %strong (coproduct completion of extensive categories)
              %br/
              While Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FreeCoproductCompletionIsExtensive"}
              says that every free coproduct completion is extensive, if a category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is already extensive to start with then its free coproduct completion may equivalently be described as the category of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundles"} bundles
              over
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              via the unique
